Z||000007||Nashco||12-09-2001||04:23 PM||||Ha, I'd never do it with Mach's rule!<P>I'd be in for it next summer <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Every summer I drive from the Ohio/Pennsylvania area to Washington...doing it with other Fieros would be fun.<P>Would this be a straight on competition to see who gets there first?  I think it would be way more fun if there were checkpoints that we met up at along the way.  Like perhaps several checkpoints along the way that are a ways off the major interstates, that somebody could get lost trying to find but if they were good with the map and driving they'd make it.<P>Also, I'd much rather it went to the west coast instead of the east coast; the west coast rules during the summer!<P>I'd seriously do this if we wanted to get together and try to make a solid plan that sounds fun.  I doubt many others would though, unfortunately; I'd love to be proved wrong though!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||87fastback||12-09-2001||05:42 PM||||I am with Nashco on this.  I think going to the West coast would much more enjoyable.  Count me in for next summer!  I think that if everyone chipped in the say $100 or $200 entry fee and got enough people together we could offer up a nice prize like a slammed 88 GT or something like that.  Using the entry money for the prizes would work, just need to get somebody to organize it.<P>Cannonball type runs have been going on for some time, and they don't "have" to be illegal.  I have been on plenty on my motorcycle and they are a blast.  We used to have prizes for the closest to actuall mileage, best time, most original ride and so forth.<P>Anyways, count me in on this one!||||reg||1
